From c331d037aa1d7abff367707a1e9282fa4cc7aeca Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kumar Anurag <kumar.singh@oss.qualcomm.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 22:51:55 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] acdb: fix status overwrite by HW Accel check in
 AcdbGetSubgraphCalibration

DataProcIsHwAccelParam() was returning its result straight into the
loop's shared status variable, which is also the value returned at
the end of AcdbGetSubgraphCalibration(). When a parameter does not
belong to the HW Accel parameter list, DataProcIsHwAccelParam()
returns AR_ENOTEXIST as the normal/expected outcome, but that value
was left in status when the loop skipped to the next <iid, pid> pair.

If this happened on the last processed parameter, the stale
AR_ENOTEXIST leaked out as the function's return value even though
every parameter was calibrated successfully, causing
AcdbGetSubgraphCalibration() to report failure.

Example: loading PARAM_ID_FNN_PLUS_MODEL succeeds (status = AR_EOK),
then PARAM_ID_FNN_PLUS_DOA_STEERING_VECTOR is not a HW Accel param
(DataProcIsHwAccelParam() = AR_ENOTEXIST), so the loop skips it via
continue without ever resetting status, and the function incorrectly
returns AR_ENOTEXIST.

Fix: store the HW Accel membership check result in a local variable
(hw_status) so it no longer overwrites the function-level status.
---
 acdb/src/acdb_command.c | 15 ++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/acdb/src/acdb_command.c b/acdb/src/acdb_command.c
index 4ad036d..b71b85d 100644
--- a/acdb/src/acdb_command.c
+++ b/acdb/src/acdb_command.c
@@ -5357,20 +5357,29 @@ int32_t AcdbGetSubgraphCalibration(AcdbAudioCalContextInfo *info,
 
         if (info->should_check_hw_accel)
         {
-            status = DataProcIsHwAccelParam(info->hw_accel_module_list_offset,
+            /*
+             * Use a local variable for the HW Accel membership check
+             * result so that the loop's running status is not
+             * overwritten by AR_ENOTEXIST when a parameter simply does
+             * not belong to the HW Accel parameter list. Leaving that
+             * result in the shared status variable caused it to leak
+             * out as the function's final return value.
+             */
+            int32_t hw_status = DataProcIsHwAccelParam(
+                info->hw_accel_module_list_offset,
                 module_header.module_iid, module_header.parameter_id);
 
             switch (mem_type)
             {
             case ACDB_HW_ACCEL_MEM_DEFAULT:
-                if (AR_SUCCEEDED(status))
+                if (AR_SUCCEEDED(hw_status))
                 {
                     cur_dot_offset += sizeof(uint32_t);
                     continue;
                 }
                 break;
             case ACDB_HW_ACCEL_MEM_CMA:
-                if (AR_FAILED(status))
+                if (AR_FAILED(hw_status))
                 {
                     cur_dot_offset += sizeof(uint32_t);
                     continue;
